 "answer_head": "# `lfu_cache.py` \u2013 A Fixed-Capacity LFU Cache with Optional Write-Back Tier\n\n```python\n\"\"\"\nlfu_cache.py\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nA fixed-capacity Least-Frequently-Used (LFU) cache with optional write-back tier\nand LRU tie-breaking for deterministic eviction.\n\nThis module implements a thread-safe LFU cache where:\n  - Eviction order is LFU with LRU tie-breaking (keys sharing the same frequency\n    are evicted in least-recently-used order).\n  - An optional write-back tier is supported via a caller-provided handler that\n    is invoked on eviction when ``write_back`` is enabled.  The handler receives\n    the ",
 "answer_tail": "tracts).\n- **Full test coverage** across eviction order, ties, write\u2011back, concurrency, and introspection.\n\nThe design prioritises clarity, determinism, and extensibility: the handler\u2011based write\u2011back tier lets the caller define what \u201cwrite\u2011back\u201d means for their specific GPU or hardware context, while the LFU\u2011LRU core ensures predictable eviction without the complexity of adaptive replacement policies. The documented failure modes guide callers toward robust integration (e.g., wrapping handlers in `try/except`, respecting the zero\u2011capacity no\u2011op, and providing handlers when `write_back=True`).",
